{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015vyzfmDijj3fPeQDzfB28N","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"6a5b489b47c58f526f9988624c0bf349ec5b75ad","date":"2026-10-07T14:56:38+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6048: Accept numeric string height in calcWeightForHeightZscore (#832)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"solomonfortune","authorEmail":"solomonbuwule@gmail.com"},{"hash":"79f2c23a1a4b3f45103fcd6f63746c87afa6e9fb","date":"2026-10-06T22:39:38+05:00","message":"(fix) O3-6046: Return null when height is outside reference table or no reference applies (#830)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-6046: Return null when height is outside reference table or no reference applies\n\n* Restore dropped weight-for-height test case\n\nThe male age4 case for 95.7 cm and 14 kg was removed along with the\nout-of-range rows, but the height is inside the reference table and\nthe expected z-score of '-1' still holds. The matching female case\nwas kept.","authorName":"Faisal Mehmood","authorEmail":"sfm7776@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fcf1b2562d60389dbf88c5383c2d4237d9d1ff8a","date":"2026-10-05T15:02:05+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-6025: Load z-score tables only when a form needs them (#824)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Load z-score reference tables only for forms that use them\n\nThe WHO reference tables behind the z-score helpers are about 1.3 MB of JSON, and zscore-service imported all eight of them statically. The form engine app imports registerExpressionHelper from the library's entry at startup, so the tables ended up in its startup chunk, and every form open downloaded and parsed them whether or not the form used a z-score helper.\n\nEach table is a dynamic import now. useProcessorDependencies loads the tables for the z-score helpers a form's schema mentions, alongside the processor's own dependencies, so they're in place before initial values or any expression is evaluated. The helpers stay synchronous, because the expression evaluator doesn't await a helper's result before applying an operator to it. getZRefByGenderAndAge is split into one function per reference, so each helper only reads the tables it needs. If a table fails to load, the form still opens, the error is reported, and the helpers that need it return null.\n\nuseProcessorDependencies also reports loading from the first render. Once a form has opened, its field adapters and concepts are cached, so initial values could otherwise be computed before the dependencies had started loading.\n\nIn esm-form-engine-app the startup chunks go from 1,189 KiB to 382 KiB, or from 301 KiB to 114 KiB gzipped.\n\n* (fix) Wait for form dependencies before evaluating growth rules\n\n* Keep form state when the schema object changes\n\nResetting the form session whenever formJson was a new object wiped\nentered values in the patient chart. esm-form-engine-app passes a new\nschema object on every render, and it re-renders once the form is\nmarked dirty, so the first edit was lost.\n\nDrop the session reset in FormFactoryProvider and stop\nuseProcessorDependencies reloading on a new formJson object. The form\nbuilder already remounts FormEngine when its schema changes, so no\nconsumer relies on replacing a mounted schema.\n\n* fix: Wait for every subform before allowing submission\n\nTrack pending dependencies by form instance so a ready sibling cannot clear another subform’s loading state. Remove the instance from the pending set when it unmounts.\n\nCover pending and failed subform dependencies, retry, required-field validation and saving all subforms after recovery.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"da88fda255243fe75f844d55c72eaf601a638d4e","date":"2026-03-04T18:39:07+03:00","message":"(feat) Expose dayjs library in expression evaluation context (#687)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Expose dayjs for date calculate expressions\n\n* pr test fixes","authorName":"Pius Rubangakene","authorEmail":"piruville@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d4222e525abbca0c78f7e444b38008075a0cf807","date":"2026-01-20T16:05:46+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve common-expression-helpers (#672)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ce5f457778e984d66d31067682e9a01a689b35cb","date":"2024-12-05T02:21:58+03:00","message":"(refactor) Tweak calcMonthsOnART helper logic (#441)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"4bca1cb1f48c9b7315306e6c560469c543315151","date":"2024-10-10T23:18:31+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Adopt OpenMRS' global Expression Runner (#409)","refs":"","body":"* Adopt the Openmrs Expression Runner\r\n\r\n* Fix mocks\r\n\r\n* Clean up","authorName":"Samuel Male","authorEmail":"samuelsmalek@gmail.com"},{"hash":"79706992d1466688cf1fc9eacf3092cbe47fb98c","date":"2024-10-03T11:07:26-07:00","message":"(fix) fixes to formatDate expression and adds tests for built-in expressions helpers (#404)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Fixes to formatDate expression and adds tests for custom expression helpers\r\n\r\n* parseDate and cleans up tests\r\n\r\n* Consume \"parseDate\" from the framework\r\n\r\n---------\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: samuelmale <samuelsmalek@gmail.com>","authorName":"Pius Rubangakene","authorEmail":"piruville@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1e744c89d3de1b3b002bc69c5492cac9ee8e6ea9","date":"2024-08-07T14:57:31+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Migrate from Formik to RHF (#349)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Samuel Male","authorEmail":"samuelsmalek@gmail.com"},{"hash":"61a28294d02423bfba356de299674eaef9f051fe","date":"2024-07-10T09:56:30+03:00","message":"(fix) Reworked logic for gravida calculation (#337)","refs":"","body":"* redo gravida logic\r\n\r\n* handle non integer values\r\n\r\n* Use Number.isInteger() over isNaN() plus JSDoc comments","authorName":"Jamie Arodi","authorEmail":"51090527+arodidev@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2045eb3d742498a58d74281eff6634f5cd1d053c","date":"2024-06-05T22:42: